From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:48:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Build with clang on Windows

clang on MinGW takes the same flags, libraries and tools as gcc there:
MSYS2 path handling, windres resources and manifests, no stack
protector, no rpath or soname. lld lacks --exclude-libs, and the
toolchain-and-OS settings given to gcc on Windows apply to clang as well.

Upstream: not submitted; part of the Windows/gcc port, not upstream OpenJDK
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
